WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.312 --> 00:00:06.121
- Hello Believe Nation, I
started the Mentor Me series

00:00:06.121 --> 00:00:08.922
with the goal to try to hang
around people who've done

00:00:08.922 --> 00:00:10.847
a lot more than us and by
sticking with them a little

00:00:10.847 --> 00:00:13.702
bit longer, hopefully some of
their ideas, their strategy

00:00:13.702 --> 00:00:16.879
their mindsets, their
beliefs seeps into us

00:00:16.879 --> 00:00:20.315
to help us become the
best version of ourselves,

00:00:20.315 --> 00:00:22.136
so today we're going to
learn from Tony Robbins

00:00:22.136 --> 00:00:24.198
and examine some of his
best motivational clips

00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:27.506
that he posted in 2016 as
an incentive for you to go

00:00:27.506 --> 00:00:29.951
for your best this year.

00:00:29.951 --> 00:00:31.273
Mentor me, Tony.

00:00:31.273 --> 00:00:33.014
Clip number one is my
personal favorite, and

00:00:33.014 --> 00:00:35.286
as always guys as Tony's
talking if he says something

00:00:35.286 --> 00:00:37.268
that really really resonates
with you, please leave

00:00:37.268 --> 00:00:38.959
in the comments below, put
quotes around it so that

00:00:38.959 --> 00:00:42.626
other people can be
inspired as well, enjoy.

00:00:56.474 --> 00:00:58.682
- The number one thing that's
going to change your life,

00:00:58.682 --> 00:01:01.645
the only thing, that
will change your life,

00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:03.799
change your business, change
your money, change your

00:01:03.799 --> 00:01:07.632
relationship, is you
must raise your standard.

00:01:08.796 --> 00:01:12.546
And I know that sounds
boring, stupid, basic,

00:01:13.588 --> 00:01:15.903
but it's the truth.

00:01:15.903 --> 00:01:18.505
The only thing that
changes our life long term,

00:01:18.505 --> 00:01:21.515
is when we raise our standards.

00:01:21.515 --> 00:01:24.866
What does that mean, that
sounds so boring and dumb.

00:01:24.866 --> 00:01:29.033
It means that all of us in
life have things we want.

00:01:31.625 --> 00:01:35.792
We don't get what we want,
we get what we have to have.

00:01:37.036 --> 00:01:37.923
Remember what I said earlier?

00:01:37.923 --> 00:01:42.090
We all get what we tolerate,
in ourselves and other people.

00:01:43.091 --> 00:01:46.352
But when you're no longer
willing to tolerate something,

00:01:46.352 --> 00:01:48.970
that's when your life changes.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:51.782
The difference in people
is their standards.

00:01:51.782 --> 00:01:52.615
Period.

00:01:53.768 --> 00:01:57.544
The difference in people
is their standards, period.

00:01:57.544 --> 00:01:59.150
And what do I mean by standards?

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:03.707
Everyone in the world
has a list of things they

00:02:03.707 --> 00:02:05.457
think they should do.

00:02:06.453 --> 00:02:07.720
I should lose weight.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.754
I should work out.

00:02:09.754 --> 00:02:12.509
I should spend more time with my kids.

00:02:12.509 --> 00:02:14.245
I should work harder.

00:02:14.245 --> 00:02:15.897
I should make more calls.

00:02:15.897 --> 00:02:19.666
I should, I should, I should, I should.

00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:21.650
And then you know what,
people don't do their shoulds

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:23.773
and they get mad at themselves
and they, what I call

00:02:23.773 --> 00:02:25.293
should all over themselves,
they beat themselves up

00:02:25.293 --> 00:02:30.016
about it, what changes
people is when your should

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.266
becomes a must.

00:02:32.612 --> 00:02:35.782
When suddenly the thing
you said should happen,

00:02:35.782 --> 00:02:37.390
has to happen.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.659
That's when human beings change.

00:02:38.659 --> 00:02:42.002
It's like if you want to take the island

00:02:42.002 --> 00:02:44.330
and you're the head of
the army and you want to

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.399
take the island, the most
powerful way to take the island

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.430
is to burn the boats.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.880
Cause if there's no way
to go back, it's amazing

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.933
what happens when it's a
must to do something versus

00:02:53.933 --> 00:02:57.146
a should, that's what
makes human beings succeed.

00:02:57.146 --> 00:02:59.934
There is another level,
the only reason you keep

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.258
saying there isn't is you
feel so exhausted about

00:03:02.258 --> 00:03:05.735
where you are, but life,
the universe or God is

00:03:05.735 --> 00:03:08.063
just testing you because
there is another level.

00:03:08.063 --> 00:03:11.961
If this is good, giant jump
to excellence, start good,

00:03:11.961 --> 00:03:14.589
poor, to good to excellence.

00:03:14.589 --> 00:03:17.955
There's a level where all
your dreams are realized.

00:03:17.955 --> 00:03:19.979
There's a level that you've
always dreamed about,

00:03:19.979 --> 00:03:23.029
it is real it has not gone away.

00:03:23.029 --> 00:03:25.616
But it takes that extra
burst when you think there's

00:03:25.616 --> 00:03:28.367
nothing left there's no
way, you've tried everything

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.734
ten million times and you keep going.

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.719
It's almost like God is
saying if you keep hitting

00:03:32.719 --> 00:03:36.228
this wall enough times I will
see that you will not stop

00:03:36.228 --> 00:03:38.425
that you are filled with
that level of determination,

00:03:38.425 --> 00:03:41.289
faith and courage and then
the door opens and you

00:03:41.289 --> 00:03:44.209
get to that next level but
most people don't know is,

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:47.959
the next level is just
two millimeters above,

00:03:48.971 --> 00:03:51.979
and it's called outstanding
ladies and gentlemen!

00:03:51.979 --> 00:03:52.994
Outstanding!

00:03:52.994 --> 00:03:54.181
(crowd cheers)

00:03:54.181 --> 00:03:55.110
What's it called?

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:56.130
- [Crowd] Outstanding!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.020
- What's it called?

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:57.954
- [Crowd] Outstanding!

00:03:57.954 --> 00:03:58.843
- What's it called?

00:03:58.843 --> 00:03:59.730
- [Crowd] Outstanding!

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:00.661
- Outstanding!

00:04:00.661 --> 00:04:01.549
Magnificent!

00:04:01.549 --> 00:04:02.523
Unstoppable!

00:04:02.523 --> 00:04:03.666
Extraordinary!

00:04:03.666 --> 00:04:07.012
Not excellent, it's a different level.

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:10.881
It's a level where you
are not one of the best,

00:04:10.881 --> 00:04:12.662
you are the best.

00:04:12.662 --> 00:04:13.590
And you know what's amazing?

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.301
You only have to be two
millimeters more than everybody

00:04:16.301 --> 00:04:17.697
else and you get everything.

00:04:17.697 --> 00:04:19.267
You get the joy, the
laughter, the fun, the family

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:22.217
the passion, the economics,
the freedom, the spirit,

00:04:22.217 --> 00:04:23.440
it's all there.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.415
What Jerry McGuire called the quan, baby.

00:04:27.415 --> 00:04:30.681
All of it, and it's just two
millimeters above and most

00:04:30.681 --> 00:04:34.365
excellent people give up
because they're exhausted

00:04:34.365 --> 00:04:36.775
and there's some people
that go the harder I hit it,

00:04:36.775 --> 00:04:39.272
the more I hit it, sooner
or later it's going down.

00:04:39.272 --> 00:04:41.895
I'm not stopping and
when you do that enough,

00:04:41.895 --> 00:04:43.206
it pops open.

00:04:43.206 --> 00:04:44.856
What makes you a leader is your
ability to make a decision,

00:04:44.856 --> 00:04:46.165
who's with me on this, right?

00:04:46.165 --> 00:04:48.280
And anybody can make the easy decision.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.462
Right, so what makes you a
leader is you can make the

00:04:51.462 --> 00:04:54.049
tough decisions and what
makes you leader is, you make

00:04:54.049 --> 00:04:55.702
the decision, what makes you
a great leader is you know

00:04:55.702 --> 00:04:57.822
I may be wrong, but if I have
to wait till everything's

00:04:57.822 --> 00:05:01.162
resolved, nothing's going to get resolved.

00:05:01.162 --> 00:05:02.711
So I'll make a decision,
if I make a decision

00:05:02.711 --> 00:05:05.838
and it's wrong I'll find
out quicker than if I sit

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.081
on the fence while my life goes by.

00:05:08.081 --> 00:05:11.047
I remember I have shared
this with maybe a few of you

00:05:11.047 --> 00:05:13.268
before but years and years
ago when we had the big

00:05:13.268 --> 00:05:16.946
Gulf War, General Norman
Schwartzkopf's a friend of mine

00:05:16.946 --> 00:05:19.301
and passed away a few years
ago, and I used to bring

00:05:19.301 --> 00:05:20.865
him in to talk about leadership.

00:05:20.865 --> 00:05:23.179
And one of the first times
I ever asked him, I said

00:05:23.179 --> 00:05:24.831
how do you define leadership?

00:05:24.831 --> 00:05:27.436
How do you know when a person's
a real leader and he said

00:05:27.436 --> 00:05:28.467
when they can make decisions.

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:31.111
I can remember when I was,
he was an assistant to a

00:05:31.111 --> 00:05:33.954
general and I forget what
the exact position is

00:05:33.954 --> 00:05:37.313
and he said he was responsible
for reading all the briefs

00:05:37.313 --> 00:05:40.447
and this general is one of the
highest generals in the army

00:05:40.447 --> 00:05:42.262
and there was a decision
that needed to be made and it

00:05:42.262 --> 00:05:45.765
had to do with ten years of
going back and forth with

00:05:45.765 --> 00:05:47.337
the Pentagon, trying to
figure out if they're going to

00:05:47.337 --> 00:05:49.708
go one direction or another,
it was a gigantic decision

00:05:49.708 --> 00:05:51.524
that was going to effect the
way the army was structured,

00:05:51.524 --> 00:05:53.297
how money was going to be divided,
what resources are going to

00:05:53.297 --> 00:05:56.274
go where, and he said they
brought in this group of

00:05:56.274 --> 00:05:59.369
20 people and they had
this two hour meeting and

00:05:59.369 --> 00:06:01.561
everybody got up and pitched
their side of what they

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:02.716
thought was right.

00:06:02.716 --> 00:06:04.366
And at the end when it
was completely done, the

00:06:04.366 --> 00:06:07.092
general said has everyone
said their piece?

00:06:07.092 --> 00:06:09.810
They said yes, he said do this.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.210
It was plan A or plan B
or whatever it was out of

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.230
the three choices that they had.

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:18.314
And everybody said okay,
general, saluted him and

00:06:18.314 --> 00:06:20.999
ran off to go implement this thing.

00:06:20.999 --> 00:06:23.599
And Schwartzkopf said he was
freaking out because he knew

00:06:23.599 --> 00:06:26.532
there was no way that general
could have read everything

00:06:26.532 --> 00:06:29.543
even he'd read, and this was
such a complex piece, and there

00:06:29.543 --> 00:06:32.026
was only two hours and
everybody gave their best, but

00:06:32.026 --> 00:06:33.932
oh my god there's so
many things to consider,

00:06:33.932 --> 00:06:36.413
and so he finally got up
enough courage he said

00:06:36.413 --> 00:06:38.886
to go to the general, and
said general, permission to

00:06:38.886 --> 00:06:40.331
speak freely?

00:06:40.331 --> 00:06:41.691
He said at ease, speak freely.

00:06:41.691 --> 00:06:44.541
He said general there is
so much information here,

00:06:44.541 --> 00:06:46.803
there's so much here no one's
going to really know for sure.

00:06:46.803 --> 00:06:50.100
How the hell could you just
make that decision like that?

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:53.909
He said because someone had to make it.

00:06:53.909 --> 00:06:56.455
He said because it's been
going around for 10 years

00:06:56.455 --> 00:06:59.811
back and forth and no one
being able to make a decision.

00:06:59.811 --> 00:07:01.445
He said what if you're wrong?

00:07:01.445 --> 00:07:04.334
He said if I'm wrong,
we'll find out quicker.

00:07:04.334 --> 00:07:07.147
If I'm right the job will be done.

00:07:07.147 --> 00:07:08.897
Next question, right?

00:07:10.535 --> 00:07:12.928
It's like when you're put
in charge, take command.

00:07:12.928 --> 00:07:15.616
Everyone in this room knows how to create.

00:07:15.616 --> 00:07:18.708
You're not a manager of your
life, you're a creator of your

00:07:18.708 --> 00:07:22.174
